A2  - Collins, M. M., Stafford, R. S., Oleary, M. P., et al., Collins, Nickel, J. C., Nickel, Robert, R. O., Lieber, M. M., Bostwick, D. G., et al., Robert
Y1  - 2006//
N2  - Objective: To investigate the effect of Sertraline combined with minocycline for the treatment of chronic prostalitis complicated with depression. <ovid:br/>Methods: A total of 90 patients with the diagnosis of chronic prostatitis complicated with depression were randomly divided into two groups. The study group received combined treatment of minocycline and Sertraline, and the control group received combined treatment of minocycline and placebo. <ovid:br/>Results: The total effective rate of chronic prostatitis of sertraline group and placebo group were 55.8% and 27.3%. The total alleviating rate of depression of sertraline group and placebo group were 79.1% and 29.5%. <ovid:br/>Conclusion: Sertraline can enhance the treatment effect of minocycline for chronic prostatitis complicated with depression. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
