Y1  - 2000//
N2  - Examined whether the postnatal blues are associated with inflammatory response system (IRS) activation. Serum concentrations of interleukin-6 (IL-6), IL-6 receptor (IL-6R), gp130 (the IL-6 signaling protein), IL-IR antagonist (IL-IRA) and leukemia inhibitory factor receptor (LIFR) were assayed in 22 nonpregnant women and in 91 pregnant women before delivery and 1-3 days after delivery. On each occasion the parturient women completed the State version of the Spielberger State-Trait-Anxiety-Inventory (STAI) and the Zung Depression Rating Scale (ZDS). Serum IL-6, IL-IRA and LIFR were significantly higher in pregnant females at the end of term than in nonpregnant females. Serum IL-6, IL-6R and IL-IRA were significantly higher and LIFR significantly lower in the early puerperium than before delivery. Women with anxiety and depressive symptoms in the puerperium are characterized by IRS activation and by a lowered anti-inflammatory activity in the serum. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
