A1  - Fernandez-Rivas, Aranzazu
A1  - Terreros, M. Teresa
A1  - Ibarmia, Joseba
A1  - Lantaron, Gaspar
A1  - Gonzalez-Torres, Miguel Angel

Y1  - 2000//
N2  - Reports the case of a 17 yr old male who in the past 4 yrs experienced 15 severe, brief depressive episodes, some of which were chronologically related to infections of the pharynx and/or tonsils and for which antibiotic therapy was the only effective treatment. Similar to the recently described pediatric autoimmune neuropsychiatric disorders associated with streptococcal infections (PANDAS), this case had a prepubertal onset and recurrent abrupt depressive onsets after symptoms suggestive of oropharyngeal infection. The patient improved rapidly only when he received antibiotics. The authors state they reported this case to increase clinicians' awareness of the possibility of a relationship between PANDAS and depressive disorders and encourage them to obtain a history of infectious diseases in patients with recurrent periods of depression. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
