A1  - Kellner, Charles H

Y1  - 1998//
N2  - A 27-yr-old woman receiving ECT for the treatment of depression developed post-ECT headaches refractory to treatment with acetaminophen and various nonsteroidal anti inflammatory drugs. The patient was then treated successfully with oral sumatriptan. This case suggests that sumatriptan may be a useful treatment of post-ECT headaches that are unresponsive to conventional analgesics. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
