T1  - Treatment of Alzheimer's disease.
T3  - American Journal of Insanity
A1  - Browning, Charles H

Y1  - 1998//
N2  - Comments on the American Psychiatric Association's (see record 1997-06277-001) practice guideline for the treatment of patients with Alzheimer's disease (AD) and other dementias of late life. The author notes that the use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) to delay the progression of AD was not recommended for lack of research, but that the side effects of NSAIDs were not mentioned. The author reports the results of a study (C. H. Browning, 1996) of psychiatric patients in which NSAIDs had psychiatric side effects including depression and suicide ideation. The author argues that clinical trials of NSAIDs should be conducted to further the understanding of the risk/benefit ratio of using these drugs to treat patients with AD. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
