A1  - Bertozzi, B
A1  - Barbisoni, P
A1  - Franzoni, S
A1  - Frisoni, G. B
A1  - Rozzini, R
A1  - Trabucchi, M

Y1  - 1996//
N2  - Investigated the effects of chronic treatment with non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAID) on cognitive status in 258 non-demented elderly patients (mean age 77.4 yrs). Ss completed the Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE), Geriatric Depression Scale, and the Instrumental Activities of Daily Living scale. 66 Ss were considered chronic NSAID users, and these Ss showed a higher MMSE score than non-users. After controlling for potential confounders in a multivariate model, chronic NSAID use remained independently associated with MMSE score. Results support a positive association between chronic NSAID use and cognitive function in non-demented elderly Ss. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
