N2  - Discusses non-pharmacologic and pharmacologic prophylactic therapies for migraine headaches. Non-pharmacological interventions include education, biofeedback, and other complementary therapies. Pharmacological agents that may be used include beta blockers, calcium channel blockers, divalproex sodium, nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs and monoamine oxidase inhibitors. Tricyclic antidepressants may be used when there are concomitant conditions such as sleep disturbance, depression, anxiety, or fibromyalgia. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
