T1  - Epidemiology of the dementias: Recent developments and new approaches.
T3  - Journal of Neurology & Psychiatry
A1  - van Duijn, C. M

Y1  - 1996//
N2  - Reviews new approaches and recent developments in the epidemiology of dementia. Descriptive studies of the occurrence across different populations and time periods as well as studies for risk factors of dementia are discussed. The different dementia-causing conditions considered include age and sex, Down's syndrome, head trauma, depression, vascular factors, anti-inflammatory drugs, smoking history, alcohol, and education. Since Alzheimer's disease (AD) is the predominant cause of dementia, accounting for at least half of the cases in most populations, epidemiological research has focused on this disorder. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
