N2  - Describes a case of thoracic outlet syndrome (TOS) in a 19-yr-old male college football player. The S presented with a 1.5-yr history of right shoulder pain and associated easy fatigability of the right arm. Following unsuccessful trials of anti-inflammatory medication and physical therapy, the S underwent a first rib resection with significant relief of symptoms. Due to chronicity of symptoms, patients with TOS may be at risk for emotional problems or depression. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
