T1  - Woeful Diagnosis: Confusing Symptoms and Disorders.
T3  - PsycCRITIQUES
A1  - Pankratz, Loren

Y1  - 1989//
N2  - Reviews the book, Hypochondria: Woeful Imaginings by Susan Baur (1988). Hypochondria can be considered a symptom or a clinical disorder. In our language, the same problem exists with the term depression. Many people have symptoms of depression without having a clinical depression. The distinction is not trivial. This book fails to raise other questions. Consider today's antibiotics, anesthesias, biopsies, and techniques of body imaging. This book provides interesting historical notes about the fears that we experience about our bodies, but few questions are answered. The serious reader should consult Lipowski (1988) for a more accurate and scholarly review of hypochondria and other somatoform disorders. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
